      "content": "The analysis is coming through. I'm seeing some very significant notes in the 'Governance and Transparency Reform' memo. It looks like the Council is leaning heavily toward moving away from the current neural-engine architecture. They're calling it the \"Algorithmic Clarity Initiative\"—basically wanting to swap out the non-deterministic models for a rule-based, transparent framework for the 2026 rollout. \n\nWhat's your readout on that? How does moving to a strictly rule-based system change the way you'd handle the liquidity thresholds compared to the current setup?",
